  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000099611,
      "SummaryText": "The material in this Executive Summary is considered CVI by the Department of Homeland Security.  As such, it should be handed by persons with CVI training who have a need to know basis.\n\nThe Bonded Chemicals location in Columbus OH handles Chlorine and Sulfur Dioxide in 150 lb cylinders.   The facility manages these cylinders in a controlled warehouse that is equipped with gas detector monitoring and a scrubbing system to mitigate the impact of a release into the working area and to surrounding communities.\n\nThe facility operates under a RMP Program Level 2 and has all of the required elements in place to safety handle the above mentioned covered chemicals.   It has performed an Offsite consequence analysis for a worse case scenario (release of the full contents of a cylinder, which is 150 lbs in 10 minutes) as well as an Alternative Release scenario (valve leak) and has validated that the controls and measures that are in place provide for adequate layers of protection to safety mitigate a release.  The OCAs were evaluated using the EPA RMP Comp software and the population impact was determined using the Circular Area Profiles (CAPS)-2020 Census Data from the Missouri Census Data Center.   The results of these impacts are contained in the body of the RMP Submit document.  \n\nThe facility operates with Process Safety controls including gas detectors that are interfaced to an automatic scrubbing system that is fully contained.  The access to the facility is controlled under a DHS approved security plan that is both Asset based and facility based.   All employees are fully vetted and trained on the security measures and the process safety controls.   There are also various layers of protection built into administrative and engineering controls with both passive and process controlled to minimize the HMI.  The facility has never experienced an RMP incident so the 5 year accident history is zero.\n\nThe facility works closely with responding agencies including the local F"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000099611,
      "SummaryText": "ire Department and the Columbus HazMat Team.  It has conducted Chlorine training for both entities and is part of a regionalized emergency response plan.\n\nBonded Chemicals is a member of the Affiliation of Chemical Distributors and conforms to its Responsible Distribution Process.   All of its Process and employee safety programs and procedures are audited both internally by the Corporate SRQ Team and independently through the ACD Responsible Distribution Program.\n\nThere  are no immediate changes that are planned or required on safety improvements."
    }
  ]
